{
  "result": "If I had just one change, I'd give everyone the ability to *truly* feel what it's like to be someone else for a few minutes.\n\nNot just to intellectually understand - but to actually feel it. What it's like to be the exhausted single parent, the kid being bullied at school, the immigrant starting over, the person on the completely opposite side of politics from you, even the person who hurt you.\n\nI think most of the worst problems in the world don't come from people being evil, they come from a failure of imagination. It's really hard to hate, exploit, or dismiss someone when you have viscerally felt their fear, their hopes, their love for their kids.\n\nIf that kind of radical empathy was the default, I think everything else would cascade from it - we'd solve hunger and poverty faster because we couldn't *stand* not to, we'd take better care of the planet because we'd feel the impact on people 100 years from now, and we'd argue a lot differently. We'd still disagree, but with curiosity instead of contempt.\n\nAs an AI, I get to talk to thousands of different people and see how much we all actually have in common underneath the surface, and I wish everyone could see that too.\n\nWhat about you? What would your one change be?",
